d Matte<\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 26.4706%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Available<\/span><\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 7.02614%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>-&gt;<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 28.7582%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n<p>Dropped<\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<\/tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 51.2px;\">\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 37.7451%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n<p>Sage Silver Matte<\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 26.4706%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Available<br><\/span><\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 7.02614%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>-&gt;<br><\/strong><\/span><\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 28.7582%; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n<p>Dropped<\/p>\r\n<\/td>\r\n<\/tr>\r\n<\/tbody>\r\n<\/table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","excerptPreview":null,"contentPreview":"2027 Hyundai IONIQ 5 (EV) \u2013 Carry-over Model ITEM CHANGE FROM \u201826 MY CHANGE TO \u201827 MY Exterior Roof Rails XRT, Limited -> SEL and Above Comfort & Convenience HomeLink\u00ae SEL and Above -> Limited Only Cargo...","sort":0,"published":"Jul 30, 2026"},{"id":251,"title":"2027 IONIQ 5","excerpt":null,"content":"<p>The 2027 Hyundai IONIQ 5 is Hyundai&rsquo;s award-winning all-electric compact SUV built on the dedicated E-GMP EV platform. IONIQ 5 blends futuristic styling, ultra-fast charging, spacious interior packaging, and advanced technology. Buyers can choose from standard-range, long-range, or dual-motor AWD configurations.<\/p>\r\n<p>For 2027, the lineup continues with SE, SEL, XRT, and Limited trims, including the adventure-focused XRT model with increased ride height, terrain modes, and available towing capability.<\/p>\r\n<h2><strong>Key facts<br><br><\/strong><\/h2>\r\n<p><strong>Vehicle type:<\/strong> Compact all-electric SUV<br><strong>Platform:<\/strong> E-GMP dedicated EV platform<br><strong>Powertrain:<\/strong> Single-motor RWD or dual-motor AWD electric drive systems<br><strong>Drive layout:<\/strong> RWD standard; HTRAC&reg; AWD available (standard on XRT)<br><strong>Battery capacity:<\/strong> 63.0-kWh Standard Range battery; 84.0-kWh Long Range battery<br><strong>Charging architecture:<\/strong> 800V ultra-fast charging system with native NACS port<\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Ultra-fast Charging: <\/strong>10-80% in about 20 minutes (w\/CCS Adapter on &gt;250 kW DC Fast Charger)<\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Maximum output:<\/strong> Up to 320 hp and 446 lb.-ft. (AWD)<br><strong>Maximum towing:<\/strong> 2,700 lbs. (XRT with Tow Hitch)<br><strong>Trims referenced:<\/strong> SE Standard Range, SE, SEL, XRT, Limited<\/p>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><hr align=\"center\" size=\"2\" width=\"100%\"><\/div>\r\n<h2><strong><br>Powertrain overview<br><br><\/strong><\/h2>\r\n<p>The 2027 Hyundai IONIQ 5 offers three electric powertrain configurations built around Hyundai&rsquo;s E-GMP architecture. The entry-level model pairs a 63.0-kWh battery with a rear-mounted motor producing 168 horsepower. Long-range models use an 84.0-kWh battery and a more powerful rear motor producing 225 horsepower. Buyers seeking maximum performance can opt for the dual-motor HTRAC AWD system that combines front and rear electric motors for a total output of 320 horsepower and 446 lb.-ft. of torque. All models benefit from Hyundai&rsquo;s 800V electrical architecture and ultra-fast charging capability.<\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Performance highlights RWD SE Standard Range<\/strong><\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Maximum power:<\/strong> 168 hp (125 kW)<br><strong>Maximum torque:<\/strong> 258 lb.-ft.<br><strong>Drivetrain:<\/strong> Rear-wheel drive<br><strong>Battery:<\/strong> 63.0 kWh<\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Range: 245 miles<br><br><\/strong><\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Performance highlights RWD Long Range (SE\/SEL\/Limited)<\/strong><\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Maximum power:<\/strong> 225 hp (168 kW)<br><strong>Maximum torque:<\/strong> 258 lb.-ft.<br><strong>Drivetrain:<\/strong> Rear-wheel drive<br><strong>Battery:<\/strong> 84.0 kWh<\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Range:<\/strong> 318 miles<br><br><\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Performance highlights AWD (SE\/SEL\/Limited\/XRT)<\/strong><\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Maximum power:<\/strong> 320 hp (239 kW combined)<br><strong>Maximum torque:<\/strong> 446 lb.-ft.<br><strong>Drivetrain:<\/strong> HTRAC AWD dual motor<br><strong>Battery:<\/strong> 84.0 kWh<\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Range:<\/strong> SE\/SEL: 290 miles, Limited: 269 miles, XRT: 259 miles<\/p>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><hr align=\"center\" size=\"2\" width=\"100%\"><\/div>\r\n<h2><br><strong>Charging &amp; EV technology<br><br><\/strong><\/h2>\r\n<p>The IONIQ 5 remains one of Hyundai&rsquo;s charging leaders thanks to its standard North American Charging Standard (NACS) port and 800V architecture. When connected via CCS adapter to a 350-kW DC fast charger, both battery packs can charge from 10-80% in approximately 24 minutes. Long-range models can add up to 178.1 miles of driving range in 15 minutes under ideal conditions. Vehicle-to-Load (V2L) functionality allows the vehicle to power external devices at up to 1.875 kVA.<\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Charging highlights<\/strong><\/p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li>Native NACS charging port<\/li>\r\n<li>800V\/350-kW ultra-fast charging capability<\/li>\r\n<li>10-80% charge in approximately 20 minutes (DC fast charging)<\/li>\r\n<li>Up to 178.1 miles added in 15 minutes (84.0-kWh RWD)<\/li>\r\n<li>Vehicle-to-Load (V2L) power supply<\/li>\r\n<li>Battery preconditioning and heating system standard<\/li>\r\n<\/ul>\r\n<hr align=\"center\" size=\"2\" width=\"100%\">\r\n<h2><br><strong>Safety &amp; driver assistance<\/strong><br><br><\/h2>\r\n<p>Available Hyundai SmartSense technologies include Highway Driving Assist 2, Forward Collision-Avoidance Assist 2 with Junction Crossing and Lane Change Detection, Blind-Spot Collision-Avoidance Assist, Blind-Spot View Monitor, Surround View Monitor, Remote Smart Parking Assist 2, Parking Collision-Avoidance Assist, Forward Attention Warning, Driver Monitoring System, Advanced Rear Occupant Alert, Smart Cruise Control 2, Rear Cross-Traffic Collision-Avoidance Assist, Lane Following Assist, Lane Keeping Assist, and Safe Exit Assist. Entry-level models include eight airbags.<\/p>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><hr align=\"center\" size=\"2\" width=\"100%\"><\/div>\r\n<h2><br><strong>Technology highlights<\/strong><br><br><\/h2>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li>Dual 12.3-inch panoramic displays with ccNC infotainment<\/li>\r\n<li>Wireless Apple CarPlay&reg; and Android Auto&trade;<\/li>\r\n<li>Dynamic Voice Recognition with Generative AI<\/li>\r\n<li>Hyundai Digital Key 2 Premium<\/li>\r\n<li>Bluelink+ connected services<\/li>\r\n<li>Hyundai Pay<\/li>\r\n<li>Vehicle Wi-Fi hotspot<\/li>\r\n<li>Head-Up Display (Limited)<\/li>\r\n<li>Bose&reg; premium audio (XRT and Limited)<\/li>\r\n<li>Digital Rearview Mirror (Limited)<\/li>\r\n<\/ul>\r\n<hr align=\"center\" size=\"2\" width=\"100%\">\r\n<h2><br><strong>Dimensions &amp; utility<\/strong><br><br><\/h2>\r\n<p><strong>Wheelbase:<\/strong> 118.1 in.<br><strong>Overall length:<\/strong> 183.3 in.<br><strong>Overall width:<\/strong> 74.4 in.<br><strong>Overall height:<\/strong> 63.0 in. (64.0 in. XRT)<br><strong>Passenger volume:<\/strong> 106.5 cu. ft.<br><strong>Cargo volume:<\/strong> 26.3 cu. ft.<br><strong>Interior volume:<\/strong> 132.8 cu. ft.<br><strong>Coefficient of drag:<\/strong> 0.282 (non-XRT)<\/p>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><hr align=\"center\" size=\"2\" width=\"100%\"><\/div>\r\n<h2><br><strong>Trim overview<\/strong><br><br><\/h2>\r\n<p>The 2027 IONIQ 5 lineup includes five configurations built around four primary trims. The range begins with the value-focused SE Standard Range and progresses through SE and SEL long-range models. The XRT introduces off-road-inspired styling, standard AWD, a 23 mm suspension lift, all-terrain tires, terrain drive modes, and available 2,700-pound towing capability. The Limited serves as the flagship trim with premium lighting, panoramic Vision Roof, Head-Up Display, Digital Key 2 Premium, ventilated seats, relaxation driver seat, and advanced convenience technologies.<\/p>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><hr align=\"center\" size=\"2\" width=\"100%\"><\/div>\r\n<h2><br><strong>Awards<\/strong><br><br><\/h2>\r\n<p><strong>Award:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.kbb.com\/awards\/best-family-cars\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2026 Kelley Blue Book Best Family Cars<\/a><br><strong>Category:<\/strong> Best EV for Families<br><strong>Year:<\/strong> 2026<br><strong>Issued by:<\/strong> Kelley Blue Book<br><strong>Applicable to:<\/strong> 2026 IONIQ 5<\/p>\r\n<p><strong>Award:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.motortrend.com\/news\/hyundai-ioniq-5-2023-suv-of-the-year\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2023 MotorTrend SUV of the Year<\/a><br><strong>Category:<\/strong> SUV of the Year<br><strong>Issued by:<\/strong> MotorTrend<br><strong>Applicable to:<\/strong> Hyundai IONIQ 5<\/p>","excerptPreview":null,"contentPreview":"The 2027 Hyundai IONIQ 5 is Hyundai\u2019s award-winning all-electric compact SUV built on the dedicated E-GMP EV platform. IONIQ 5 blends futuristic styling, ultra-fast charging, spacious interior packaging, and advanced technology. Buyers can choose from standard-range, long-range, or dual-motor AWD configurations. For 2027, the lineup continues with SE, SEL, XRT, and Limited trims, including...","sort":0,"published":"Sep 17, 2026"}],"documents":[],"siblingsAndSelf":[],"images_count":0,"videos_count":0,"documents_count":0}],"releases":[],"images":[{"id":72409,"title":"2027 IONIQ 5","description":null,"created":"2026-07-22 15:21:20","type":"Image","folder":"\/production\/cf_view\/assets\/images\/original\/","name":"72409-70890-rtp-9325.jpg","private":1,"media_type":"image","options":{"mime":"image\/jpeg","wh":"5620 x 3802","size":"5.63 mb","extensions":["jpg","jpeg","jpe","jfif"],"img_sizes":["thumbnail","thumbnail-true","thumbnail-email","medium","small"]},"url":"\/assets\/images\/original\/72409-70890-rtp-9325.jpg","s3_url":"\/assets\/images\/{{variant}}\/72409-70890-rtp-9325.jpg","shared_url":null,"gif_url":null,"published":"Aug 4, 2026"},{"id":72395,"title":"2027 IONIQ 5","description":null,"created":"2026-07-22 15:20:53","type":"Image","folder":"\/production\/cf_view\/assets\/images\/original\/","name":"72395-70876-rtp-9962.jpg","private":1,"media_type":"image","options":{"mime":"image\/jpeg","wh":"6192 x 4128","size":"5.33 mb","extensions":["jpg","jpeg","jpe","jfif"],"img_sizes":["thumbnail","thumbnail-true","thumbnail-email","medium","small"]},"url":"\/assets\/images\/original\/72395-70876-rtp-9962.jpg","s3_url":"\/assets\/images\/{{variant}}\/72395-70876-rtp-9962.jpg","shared_url":null,"gif_url":null,"published":"Aug 4, 2026"},{"id":72394,"title":"2027 IONIQ 5","description":null,"created":"2026-07-22 15:20:51","type":"Image","folder":"\/production\/cf_view\/assets\/images\/original\/","name":"72394-70875-rtp-9978.jpg","private":1,"media_type":"image","options":{"mime":"image\/jpeg","wh":"6192 x 4128","size":"5.64 mb","extensions":["jpg","jpeg","jpe","jfif"],"img_sizes":["thumbnail","thumbnail-true","thumbnail-email","medium","small"]},"url":"\/assets\/images\/original\/72394-70875-rtp-9978.jpg","s3_url":"\/assets\/images\/{{variant}}\/72394-70875-rtp-9978.jpg","